    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's what I did and why it keeps structural impact low.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: `POST /api/owners` may include a `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR); `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given. Since GET reloads from the database, `title` has to persist.\n\nI added the behaviour as small, cohesive units rather than growing any existing method:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` to the `OwnerFields` input schema and a read-only `salutation` to the `Owner` output schema. MapStruct auto-maps `title` (matching name) into the entity; the generated DTOs pick up both fields.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 a new `title` field plus its own `getTitle`/`setTitle`. New self-contained accessors; no existing method touched.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one new `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` deriving `salutation` inline, exactly like the existing `displayName`/`initials` derivations. No method body changed.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** (the test profile runs `ddl-auto=none`) \u2014 a `title` column, appended at the end of `owners` so the positional seed inserts stay aligned.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended a `NULL` title to the 10 seed rows to match the new column count.\n\nI only touched the hsqldb schema because that's the test profile; the app's h2 profile runs `ddl-auto=update` and creates the column automatically, so no extra schema files were needed.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS` (the new `coreComposesSalutation` returns `\"DR who\"`, and the suite's sole test class passes).",
